      "content": "That's an interesting way to frame it. You mentioned local officials being influenced by goblins or new goblins being appointed—are you saying that merchants actually believed these disruptions were caused by literal creatures, or are you using that as a metaphor for the chaotic nature of the trade routes? \n\nI'd love to hear more about those \"low-level disasters\" you listed, especially the ones involving communication and the administrative side of things. What other kinds of small, seemingly random losses or \"bad luck\" events did merchants deal with?",
      "source": "evaluator"
